-- cmd: repl
-- stderr-contains: expected expression, found |>
-- stdin: import list\n[1, 2]\n  |> list.length\n[1, 2] |>\n  list.length\n([1, 2]\n  |> list.length)\n:quit\n
-- The REPL runs an input as soon as it is complete, so a line that
-- starts with `|>` is a new input; a line that ends in `|>`, or the
-- pipeline in parentheses, goes on.
